{"path":"error/errno_macros","title":"Error numbers","titleHtml":"Error numbers","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/c/error/errno_macros","section":"error","kind":"page","summary":"Each of the macros defined in <errno.h> expands to an integer constant expression with type int and with a unique positive value.","html":"<p>Each of the macros defined in <a href=\"/w/c/error\"><code>&lt;errno.h&gt;</code></a> expands to an integer constant expression with type <span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">int</span></span> and with a unique positive value. The following constants are defined by ISO C. The implementation may define more, as long as they begin with <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"st0\">'E'</span></span></code> followed by digits or uppercase letters.\n</p>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/c/error\"><code>&lt;errno.h&gt;</code></a></code> </div>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span>EDOM</span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  Mathematics argument out of domain of function <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(macro constant)</span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span>EILSEQ</span></span></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c95\">(C95)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  Illegal byte sequence <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(macro constant)</span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span>ERANGE</span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  Result too large <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(macro constant)</span>\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>Many additional errno constants are <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://pubs.opengroup.org/onlinepubs/9699919799/basedefs/errno.h.html\" data-external=\"1\">defined by POSIX</a> and by the <a href=\"/w/cpp/error/errno_macros\">C++ standard library</a>, and individual implementations may define even more, e.g. <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw2\">errno</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">3</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> on Linux or <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">intro<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">2</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> on BSD and OS X.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"c\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;errno.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;math.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;string.h&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw2\">errno</span> <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw773\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"log(-1.0) =&nbsp;%f<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>, <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/math/log\"><span class=\"kw582\">log</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu16\">1.0</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw773\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"%s<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span><span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>, <a href=\"/w/c/string/byte/strerror\"><span class=\"kw496\">strerror</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw2\">errno</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw2\">errno</span> <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw773\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"log(0.0)  =&nbsp;%f<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>, <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/math/log\"><span class=\"kw582\">log</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu16\">0.0</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw773\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"%s<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>, <a href=\"/w/c/string/byte/strerror\"><span class=\"kw496\">strerror</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw2\">errno</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Possible output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>log(-1.0) = nan\nNumerical argument out of domain\n&nbsp;\nlog(0.0)  = -inf\nNumerical result out of range</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"References\">References</h3>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-23\">\n<ul><li> C23 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:2024): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.5/2 Errors &lt;errno.h&gt; (p: TBD)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-17\">\n<ul><li> C17 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:2018): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.5/2 Errors &lt;errno.h&gt; (p: TBD)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-11\">\n<ul><li> C11 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:2011): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.5/2 Errors &lt;errno.h&gt; (p: 205)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-c99\">\n<ul><li> C99 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:1999): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.5/2 Errors &lt;errno.h&gt; (p: 186)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-c89\">\n<ul><li> C89/C90 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:1990): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 4.1.3 Errors &lt;errno.h&gt; \n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/c/error/errno\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>errno</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  macro which expands to POSIX-compatible thread-local error number variable<br><span class=\"t-mark\">(macro variable)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/c/io/perror\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>perror</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   displays a character string corresponding of the current error to <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/c/io/std_streams\">stderr</a></span> <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/c/string/byte/strerror\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>strerror</span><span>strerror_s</span><span>strerrorlen_s</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c11\">(C11)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c11\">(C11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   returns a text version of a given error code <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div class=\"t-dsc-see\"><span><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/errno_macros\">C++ documentation</a></span> for <span><span>Error numbers</span></span></div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"References","id":"References"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C reference"},{"path":"error","title":"Error handling"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"Error numbers","children":[{"label":"Entries","children":[{"label":"EDOM","note":"Mathematics argument out of domain of function"},{"label":"EILSEQ","note":"Illegal byte sequence"},{"label":"ERANGE","note":"Result too large"}]},{"label":"Notes","note":"Many additional errno constants are defined by POSIX and by the C++ standard library, and individual implementations may define even more, e.g. errno(3) on…"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"errno","note":"macro which expands to POSIX-compatible thread-local error number variable"},{"label":"perror","note":"displays a character string corresponding of the current error to stderr"},{"label":"strerror, strerror_s, strerrorlen_s","note":"returns a text version of a given error code"}]}]},"standards":["C95","C11"],"wordCount":242,"codeBlockCount":2}
